      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "Benday.EfCore.SqlServer.DomainModels.CoreFieldsDomainModelBase",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Benday.EfCore.SqlServer.DomainModels.CoreFieldsDomainModelBase.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Domain model base class with audit fields and optimistic concurrency.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/Benday.EfCore.SqlServer.DomainModels.CoreFieldsDomainModelBase.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"3\">The Timestamp property carries the concurrency token across the\nadapter boundary so the service layer can detect conflicting updates\nwithout touching the entity layer directly.</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/Benday.EfCore.SqlServer.DomainModels.DomainModelBase.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/Benday.EfCore.SqlServer.DomainModels.DomainModelBase.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "Benday.EfCore.SqlServer.DomainModels.DomainModelBase",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Benday.EfCore.SqlServer.DomainModels.DomainModelBase.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Base class for domain models. Uses IEntityIdentity{int} from\nthe shared interface package so domain models and entities\nshare the same identity contract.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/Benday.EfCore.SqlServer.DomainModels.DomainModelBase.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"5\">Domain models are NOT EF Core entities. They live on the business\nlogic side of the adapter boundary. EF Core should never see these.</p>\n"
    },
